+- Extinction coefficient function $\sigma_{\mathrm{t}}(\mathbf{x}, \omega)$, which returns the total extinction coefficient at position $\mathbf{x}$ for direction $\omega$. This function may depend on position and direction, though often $\omega$ is fixed for a single ray segment.
 
 **Outputs:**
-- Transmittance $\mathcal{T} (\mathrm{p} \to \mathrm{p}^\prime)$: A scalar in $[0, 1]$ representing the fraction of radiance transmitted [S2, unofficial].
-- Optical depth $\tau (\mathrm{p} \to \mathrm{p}^\prime)$: A scalar representing the accumulated extinction along the path [S2, unofficial].
